>Chameleon liches are not impossible (sucked it to one at minesend).

Indeed. But, they're very unusual.

>Ki-rins and angels start appearing around levels 15 and 20 (got both).

Angels are not wizardly spellcasters.

Titans, master liches, ki-rin, and Archons *are*, but are not high
enough level to cast touch of death unless they receive bonus hit dice.

>Guaranteed spellcasters include the titan on Medusa's ruins and many of 
>quest nemeses (it was nice meeting one of the latter).

A cursory inspection of the monster database reveals that no wizardly
quest nemesis has more than 16 hit dice; no monster with fewer than 21
hit dice can cast touch of death at all.

In short: in vanilla, you cannot be touch-of-death'd by a random monster
unless you are desperately unlucky (chameleon or polymorph magic yielding
an archlich) or desperately stupid (entering Gehennom without magic 
resistance).
